1
00:00:05,837 --> 00:00:07,234
(All characters, places, and organizations
in this drama are fictitious.)

2
00:00:07,234 --> 00:00:08,791
(Filming followed broadcast guidelines
for minors, some scenes used AI.)

3
00:00:17,231 --> 00:00:19,461
(Episode 24)

4
00:00:21,518 --> 00:00:24,718
I forgot to give this back last night.

5
00:00:25,551 --> 00:00:27,351
Where did you find this?

6
00:00:27,718 --> 00:00:29,765
It was the nicest thing
in the whole house,

7
00:00:29,790 --> 00:00:31,872
so why'd you shove it
in the back of the cupboard?

8
00:00:35,151 --> 00:00:36,884
Because your mom gave it to you?

9
00:00:38,718 --> 00:00:40,769
I heard it from that old lady
you work for.

10
00:00:41,751 --> 00:00:44,618
She hid that she was your mom
and dropped off lunch?

11
00:00:45,151 --> 00:00:48,751
Is she an undercover royal inspector?
That damn woman.

12
00:00:53,184 --> 00:00:56,884
The Ms. Hong I told you about?
I don't think she's the one.

13
00:00:58,118 --> 00:01:02,584
She's not the real deal either.
She just pigged out on the kimchi.

14
00:01:05,984 --> 00:01:08,584
Maybe it's because I took
that cursed lunchbox out with me...

15
00:01:12,351 --> 00:01:17,484
Even if I end it,
I'm having premium grouper first.

16
00:01:29,291 --> 00:01:31,853
It's a waiver of your assets,
inheritance, and gifts.

17
00:01:34,118 --> 00:01:38,718
Anything could happen to me,
so I want to do this by the book.

18
00:01:41,604 --> 00:01:44,671
It means forfeiting all stocks,
real estate, savings, deposits, and cash,

19
00:01:45,084 --> 00:01:48,084
every asset you could inherit from me,

20
00:01:49,784 --> 00:01:55,918
along with any right to manage
or inherit the family business,

21
00:01:56,218 --> 00:02:01,084
take an executive role, or hold assets
in your parents' names.

22
00:02:01,884 --> 00:02:02,984
Mom.

23
00:02:03,684 --> 00:02:04,751
Please sign here.

24
00:02:07,151 --> 00:02:10,751
From now on, Yun Jin
will take over the company too.

25
00:02:11,484 --> 00:02:13,951
- Ma'am.
- Okay.

26
00:02:14,218 --> 00:02:16,284
Even if you're starving,
you won't get a single cent.

27
00:02:17,651 --> 00:02:18,684
Okay.

28
00:02:21,118 --> 00:02:22,984
I won't ask for anything else,

29
00:02:25,518 --> 00:02:27,318
but when I come home, cook me a meal.

30
00:02:29,018 --> 00:02:34,118
You've walked on red carpets since birth,
so you don't know what mud is like.

31
00:02:34,551 --> 00:02:38,818
Only those who've walked through mud
and over gravel can handle it. You can't.

32
00:02:40,918 --> 00:02:42,584
That's how I raised you.

33
00:02:43,184 --> 00:02:46,651
You've had the best of everything.
You know what it's like,

34
00:02:48,418 --> 00:02:51,718
so soon you'll be dying
to get back on that carpet.

35
00:02:53,884 --> 00:02:58,584
Thanks to you, Mother,
I've lived life on the carpet.

36
00:02:59,018 --> 00:03:02,384
And because I know it so well,
I don't miss it at all.

37
00:03:03,018 --> 00:03:05,918
Mud, gravel. None of it scares me.

38
00:03:06,351 --> 00:03:09,151
I know what makes me happy, Mother.

39
00:03:09,984 --> 00:03:12,484
Will Han Gyu Rim feel the same way?

40
00:03:15,618 --> 00:03:19,118
She probably thought being with you
meant a life on the red carpet.

41
00:03:19,684 --> 00:03:22,084
Will she hold on to you,
who have nothing to your name,

42
00:03:23,103 --> 00:03:25,917
and love you like she does now?

43
00:03:30,451 --> 00:03:34,651
Even if we walk through gravel
and mud worse than this,

44
00:03:35,904 --> 00:03:38,171
Gyu Rim will never let go of my hand.

45
00:03:39,618 --> 00:03:40,684
Want to bet?

46
00:03:51,536 --> 00:03:55,695
(Notice, Closed for one week
for renovations.)

47
00:03:57,444 --> 00:03:59,054
You're here, ma'am?

48
00:03:59,527 --> 00:04:01,413
Could you come to the kitchen?

49
00:04:02,218 --> 00:04:05,918
On your way, could you bring me
the container for the radish kimchi?

50
00:04:16,451 --> 00:04:18,463
I'm so hungry, Gyu Rim.

51
00:04:20,237 --> 00:04:22,250
Can't you eat with me?

52
00:04:53,251 --> 00:04:56,526
You had breakfast, right?
Still, have at least a bite.

53
00:04:56,851 --> 00:04:58,591
The hangover soup here is amazing.

54
00:05:01,131 --> 00:05:03,374
Did you drink a lot
at the reunion yesterday?

55
00:05:05,418 --> 00:05:07,143
You look so worn out.

56
00:05:09,497 --> 00:05:12,564
Right? I look half dead today, don't I?

57
00:05:15,218 --> 00:05:17,526
Did something happen? Are you sick?

58
00:05:20,684 --> 00:05:25,084
I'm so happy, it's killing me.

59
00:05:28,884 --> 00:05:32,218
My mother gave us her blessing.

60
00:05:33,718 --> 00:05:34,818
You're lying.

61
00:05:36,151 --> 00:05:37,751
Why would I lie to you about that?

62
00:05:38,018 --> 00:05:39,939
How did this happen so fast...

63
00:05:40,732 --> 00:05:42,739
You said it would take some time.

64
00:05:43,651 --> 00:05:47,418
I thought it would,
but somehow it just worked out.

65
00:05:48,584 --> 00:05:50,070
I even made up with my mother.

66
00:05:50,223 --> 00:05:52,423
She said she'll feed me when I go home.

67
00:05:56,551 --> 00:06:01,318
So from now on,
let's love each other all we want.

68
00:06:02,084 --> 00:06:05,551
If you like me 100 percent,
show me all 100.

69
00:06:05,584 --> 00:06:10,784
Don't hold back, don't hide it,
and don't leave anything out. Got it?

70
00:06:43,177 --> 00:06:46,477
Gyu Yeong, Han Gyu Yeong...

71
00:06:47,838 --> 00:06:50,148
How did you end up like this?

72
00:06:56,518 --> 00:06:58,839
Kang Seong Uk, you con artist!

73
00:07:00,384 --> 00:07:03,551
Kang Seong Uk, you con artist!

74
00:07:19,081 --> 00:07:22,937
I'm so shocked,
I don't even know what to say...

75
00:07:24,986 --> 00:07:30,364
So you're the one
who did that to that vixen?

76
00:07:31,244 --> 00:07:32,373
Yeah.

77
00:07:33,213 --> 00:07:37,760
I didn't know my finger
was that strong either.

78
00:07:38,284 --> 00:07:42,651
She was being so annoying
that I flicked her forehead just once.

79
00:07:43,151 --> 00:07:45,418
And she passed out right away.

80
00:07:45,884 --> 00:07:51,051
A little later, she came to
and looked at me all clear-eyed,

81
00:07:51,251 --> 00:07:57,351
then suddenly said, "Who are you?"
She'd totally lost it.

82
00:07:57,551 --> 00:08:02,118
Why would you flick a girl's forehead?
What for?

83
00:08:02,584 --> 00:08:06,884
It hasn't been long since you paid up
for "one punch, six teeth."

84
00:08:07,484 --> 00:08:10,984
Did you already forget
what kind of fist you have?

85
00:08:11,451 --> 00:08:16,596
So if the police get involved this time,
I'll end up in handcuffs.

86
00:08:17,384 --> 00:08:21,451
So I couldn't call her family,
and I brought her here instead.

87
00:08:21,551 --> 00:08:24,084
You should just get handcuffed, you idiot.

88
00:08:25,284 --> 00:08:29,584
You think I'd live under the same roof
with you, scared you'll hit me?

89
00:08:30,551 --> 00:08:31,915
Which finger was it?

90
00:08:32,016 --> 00:08:34,086
I'll snap it right off,

91
00:08:34,118 --> 00:08:35,884
so point to which one it was.

92
00:08:35,909 --> 00:08:38,376
Snap them all off.

93
00:08:38,651 --> 00:08:42,351
If snapping my fingers would fix it,
I'd have done it a hundred times.

94
00:08:43,498 --> 00:08:45,808
I'm scared of myself too, Mom.

95
00:08:46,865 --> 00:08:51,830
They say an enemy from your past life
comes back as your child.

96
00:08:51,864 --> 00:08:53,617
An enemy from your past life...

97
00:08:56,084 --> 00:08:59,884
Still, the doctor at the hospital said...

98
00:09:01,318 --> 00:09:05,451
it's temporary memory loss
from a strong blow,

99
00:09:05,818 --> 00:09:09,651
and that her memory should return
within a month, so not to worry.

100
00:09:12,284 --> 00:09:14,251
At least that's some good news.

101
00:09:15,284 --> 00:09:17,513
So what now?

102
00:09:18,173 --> 00:09:19,659
What are you going to do?

103
00:09:19,684 --> 00:09:23,584
Are you just going to keep
that vixen here at home?

104
00:09:24,284 --> 00:09:27,051
Just until her memory comes back.

105
00:09:28,057 --> 00:09:33,290
They said a month at most, so it might be
back tonight or tomorrow, right?

106
00:09:33,384 --> 00:09:36,518
Won't her in-laws come looking for her?

107
00:09:38,818 --> 00:09:43,118
Her in-laws think she's on a business trip
to the States, so that's fine,

108
00:09:44,037 --> 00:09:46,817
but we can't ever tell her family.

109
00:09:47,084 --> 00:09:50,751
If Gyu Rim knew I did this to Gyu Yeong,
she'd faint on the spot.

110
00:09:50,870 --> 00:09:52,390
And her father...

111
00:09:52,730 --> 00:09:55,477
I don't even want to think about it.

112
00:09:55,751 --> 00:09:59,784
If Han Seok Jung finds out,
he'll make your ears bleed that very day,

113
00:09:59,818 --> 00:10:02,051
and you'll shrivel up and die.

114
00:10:02,218 --> 00:10:04,418
You think I'm some idiot?

115
00:10:04,784 --> 00:10:05,818
Sister.

116
00:10:08,751 --> 00:10:10,584
You're finally up?

117
00:10:10,618 --> 00:10:13,084
Yes, I'm up. I'm thirsty, Sister.

118
00:10:13,651 --> 00:10:15,484
- Water.
- Water.

119
00:10:16,418 --> 00:10:20,084
Sit down here. Have a seat.

120
00:10:20,110 --> 00:10:21,110
Okay.

121
00:10:25,184 --> 00:10:26,918
- Drink some water.
- Thank you.

122
00:10:28,984 --> 00:10:30,184
Who are you?

123
00:10:31,351 --> 00:10:37,818
I mean, who do you think you might be?

124
00:10:40,518 --> 00:10:41,584
I don't know.

125
00:10:42,718 --> 00:10:44,500
How can you not know?

126
00:10:44,640 --> 00:10:47,207
It's not like his fist is made of iron.

127
00:10:47,451 --> 00:10:49,384
Just because he flicked you wrong,

128
00:10:49,584 --> 00:10:52,884
how can you not even know who you are?

129
00:10:53,484 --> 00:10:55,884
- I'm scared. Sister scares me.
- Fine.

130
00:10:56,184 --> 00:10:59,618
"Sister," my foot. How am I your "sister?"

131
00:10:59,951 --> 00:11:04,718
Hey, if my first love hadn't failed,
I'd have a grandkid your age.

132
00:11:05,684 --> 00:11:07,851
Call her Granny.

133
00:11:08,084 --> 00:11:11,484
You were always rude,
so you called my mom "Granny."

134
00:11:12,784 --> 00:11:15,384
That granny scares me. Tell her to leave.

135
00:11:15,666 --> 00:11:17,111
Is this your house?

136
00:11:17,584 --> 00:11:21,218
It's my house, and I'm in it.
Who are you to tell me to leave?

137
00:11:22,051 --> 00:11:26,151
What if she gets another shock
and never gets her memory back?

138
00:11:27,284 --> 00:11:30,151
Just go to the store already.
Lee Guk's waiting.

139
00:11:31,351 --> 00:11:36,584
Unbelievable. I'd rather die
than deal with this.

140
00:11:45,818 --> 00:11:46,851
She's gone.

141
00:11:50,551 --> 00:11:52,484
I told you I wasn't coming here.

142
00:11:53,118 --> 00:11:57,384
Your mom already has it out for me
more than anyone.

143
00:11:57,651 --> 00:11:59,218
It's like walking into a lion's den...

144
00:11:59,418 --> 00:12:02,051
Did you have anywhere else to go?

145
00:12:03,351 --> 00:12:07,984
Swallow your pride and go home already.

146
00:12:09,158 --> 00:12:13,991
No matter what you do, your family's
the only one who'll take you back.

147
00:12:14,518 --> 00:12:16,418
I told you I'm not going there.

148
00:12:16,584 --> 00:12:19,818
I can show everyone in the world
what a mess I've become,

149
00:12:20,284 --> 00:12:23,051
but not my family. Never.

150
00:12:28,984 --> 00:12:32,718
Hey. Your friend called you.

151
00:12:33,897 --> 00:12:36,764
Su Chan? Yeah, Song Su Chan.

152
00:12:36,918 --> 00:12:40,718
He said he'd give you half the stake
in his clothing store,

153
00:12:40,851 --> 00:12:42,818
but you turned it down?

154
00:12:43,918 --> 00:12:46,118
He asked me to talk you into it.

155
00:12:46,184 --> 00:12:47,984
Why did you answer my phone?

156
00:12:48,009 --> 00:12:50,392
You punk. Am I a stranger?
I'm your father.

157
00:12:52,031 --> 00:12:54,198
You've got nothing.
Why would you turn it down?

158
00:12:55,051 --> 00:12:58,118
He said you even saved his life.

159
00:12:58,551 --> 00:13:04,018
If you did something that big,
a whole store wouldn't be enough.

160
00:13:05,951 --> 00:13:09,284
You're not getting any younger.

161
00:13:09,951 --> 00:13:13,518
How long will you suck up to drunks,
get hit with broken bottles,

162
00:13:13,651 --> 00:13:15,084
and live as a waiter?

163
00:13:16,818 --> 00:13:17,851
A waiter?

164
00:13:18,984 --> 00:13:20,151
I know, you punk.

165
00:13:21,384 --> 00:13:24,418
That you've been making a living
as a waiter.

166
00:13:25,318 --> 00:13:30,584
Back when Gyu Seo said you did rough work,
I figured it out right away.

167
00:13:32,318 --> 00:13:36,118
You never got an education,
but you're good-looking,

168
00:13:36,651 --> 00:13:39,884
handsome like me,
so I figured you were working as a waiter.

169
00:13:41,551 --> 00:13:48,218
My friend says a popular waiter makes
way more in tips than his salary.

170
00:13:48,884 --> 00:13:50,116
So?

171
00:13:50,623 --> 00:13:54,850
So because it was tips, you just took it
without feeling bad at all?

172
00:13:56,956 --> 00:14:00,308
Of course I felt bad.

173
00:14:01,084 --> 00:14:04,261
It hurt me too. I just didn't show it.

174
00:14:04,361 --> 00:14:06,008
I didn't want to make
things harder for you.

175
00:14:08,918 --> 00:14:14,651
Anyway, owning a clothing store beats
being a waiter a thousand times over.

176
00:14:14,684 --> 00:14:16,284
I wasn't a waiter. I was a gigolo.

177
00:14:17,944 --> 00:14:18,944
What?

178
00:14:19,224 --> 00:14:21,857
A gigolo who seduces women
and takes their money.

179
00:14:25,678 --> 00:14:27,695
No matter how much a waiter makes in tips,

180
00:14:27,818 --> 00:14:32,551
how could I keep cleaning up your messes
and earn that much money?

181
00:14:35,551 --> 00:14:38,884
Gyu Rim doesn't know.
As long as she doesn't, it's fine.

182
00:14:39,751 --> 00:14:43,751
Even if the rest of the family knows,
Gyu Rim can't ever find out.

183
00:15:02,984 --> 00:15:04,384
My eldest son, a gigolo?

184
00:15:08,617 --> 00:15:10,350
And I took the money he made from that?

185
00:15:17,418 --> 00:15:18,718
What kind of father...

186
00:15:24,651 --> 00:15:26,084
Here, say "ah."

187
00:15:29,670 --> 00:15:30,670
Okay.

188
00:15:32,777 --> 00:15:34,510
It tastes even better.

189
00:15:38,384 --> 00:15:40,251
I think you got a text.

190
00:15:41,097 --> 00:15:44,130
It's fine. I'll check it after I feed you.

191
00:15:47,363 --> 00:15:48,397
Here, "ah."

192
00:15:51,584 --> 00:15:55,218
I'm going to the office after I eat,
so don't mind me and go do your thing.

193
00:15:55,251 --> 00:15:57,073
Where are you going like this?

194
00:15:57,818 --> 00:15:59,418
I told you, I'm really fine.

195
00:16:00,984 --> 00:16:02,218
Hun Tae.

196
00:16:02,251 --> 00:16:06,684
Honey, being here with you like this,

197
00:16:07,584 --> 00:16:11,418
all I want to do is hold on to you.

198
00:16:14,284 --> 00:16:18,418
I want to beg you not to go anywhere
and to stay by my side.

199
00:16:20,318 --> 00:16:21,603
I'll do better.

200
00:16:23,110 --> 00:16:24,963
Much better than I do now.

201
00:16:26,184 --> 00:16:30,284
So can't you let me hold on to you?

202
00:16:36,142 --> 00:16:37,709
You poor man.

203
00:16:42,397 --> 00:16:47,951
Someone as great as you
deserves a much better woman.

204
00:16:49,384 --> 00:16:55,484
How could someone so perfect
have such bad taste in women?

205
00:16:57,931 --> 00:16:59,286
That's not true.

206
00:16:59,980 --> 00:17:04,033
The proudest moment of my life...

207
00:17:04,418 --> 00:17:06,651
was meeting you.

208
00:17:11,918 --> 00:17:13,184
Answer it.

209
00:17:22,334 --> 00:17:24,788
Why? It might be urgent. Answer it.

210
00:17:26,668 --> 00:17:27,927
No.

211
00:17:29,928 --> 00:17:30,968
I don't have to.

212
00:17:32,934 --> 00:17:34,527
It might be urgent.

213
00:17:39,181 --> 00:17:40,208
I forgot too.

214
00:17:40,561 --> 00:17:42,064
I need to call Director Kim.

215
00:17:42,445 --> 00:17:43,445
Just a moment.

216
00:17:43,848 --> 00:17:46,227
- You didn't even finish eating.
- It's fine.

217
00:18:03,001 --> 00:18:05,007
Why didn't you answer the phone?

218
00:18:05,321 --> 00:18:07,134
I texted you too,
but you didn't even read it.

219
00:18:09,741 --> 00:18:10,741
Why are you crying?

220
00:18:12,290 --> 00:18:14,347
Did something happen to the kids?

221
00:18:15,154 --> 00:18:16,386
What do I do, honey?

222
00:18:16,411 --> 00:18:20,821
Our eldest son, our Gyu O,
they say he's a gigolo.

223
00:18:21,568 --> 00:18:26,361
A gigolo who swindles rich women.
Our Gyu O.

224
00:18:31,154 --> 00:18:32,724
What?

225
00:18:34,699 --> 00:18:36,494
What did Gyu O do?

226
00:18:59,619 --> 00:19:00,747
Hello?

227
00:19:03,266 --> 00:19:04,756
Yes, go ahead.

228
00:19:05,661 --> 00:19:07,517
Is this Han Gyu O's phone?

229
00:19:09,693 --> 00:19:12,168
Yes. Who is this?

230
00:19:14,360 --> 00:19:17,183
Gyu O. It's Mom.

231
00:20:03,701 --> 00:20:07,325
I'm Han Gyu O. How have you been?

232
00:20:12,220 --> 00:20:13,220
Mom.

233
00:20:17,334 --> 00:20:19,317
Why couldn't you live a better life?

234
00:20:21,567 --> 00:20:24,471
Why couldn't you have lived any better?

235
00:20:30,506 --> 00:20:32,288
Plenty of kids whose moms left home,

236
00:20:32,474 --> 00:20:36,141
or who weren't raised by their moms,
don't end up like you.

237
00:20:38,566 --> 00:20:41,687
Even if they grew up
in unbelievably rough conditions,

238
00:20:41,968 --> 00:20:45,246
even if their parents abandoned them,

239
00:20:45,393 --> 00:20:49,779
even if they were raised by scum
who can't even be called parents,

240
00:20:50,331 --> 00:20:54,967
countless kids still turn out
good and decent.

241
00:21:14,568 --> 00:21:15,826
My Gyu O...

242
00:21:17,809 --> 00:21:21,068
You were such a good kid.

243
00:21:21,780 --> 00:21:24,375
You were so kind and hardworking,

244
00:21:25,045 --> 00:21:29,441
so honest and well-behaved.

245
00:21:33,201 --> 00:21:37,928
You were such a wonderful kid!

246
00:22:18,313 --> 00:22:20,867
I didn't hit you
because I have the right to.

247
00:22:23,707 --> 00:22:25,345
How dare I...

248
00:22:30,168 --> 00:22:32,268
I know I have no right to do this...

249
00:22:32,281 --> 00:22:33,781
I know you must be ashamed of me.

250
00:22:42,073 --> 00:22:43,887
I didn't live the right way,

251
00:22:45,785 --> 00:22:47,941
but I've always worked hard.

252
00:22:51,847 --> 00:22:56,448
It's been that way since you left,
and it still is.

253
00:22:58,594 --> 00:23:01,684
I've never once held back
in my whole life.

254
00:23:05,054 --> 00:23:07,188
I worked myself to death too.

255
00:23:33,869 --> 00:23:35,367
Anyway, I'm sorry.

256
00:23:37,688 --> 00:23:39,441
From now on, I'll live a good life,

257
00:23:41,598 --> 00:23:43,001
so you won't have to worry about me.

258
00:23:48,947 --> 00:23:50,789
I'm sorry, Gyu O.

259
00:23:56,094 --> 00:23:57,381
Gyu O.

260
00:23:59,920 --> 00:24:01,773
I'm so sorry.

261
00:24:03,768 --> 00:24:06,488
I'm so sorry, Gyu O.

262
00:24:57,145 --> 00:24:58,394
Su Chan.

263
00:25:01,701 --> 00:25:02,968
I'll take your offer.

264
00:25:04,574 --> 00:25:08,536
Give me half the stake
in your clothing store.

265
00:25:12,762 --> 00:25:14,328
(Damga Charcoal Grill)

266
00:25:19,826 --> 00:25:22,650
A bottle of soju here, please.

267
00:25:35,081 --> 00:25:36,081
What is it?

268
00:25:36,231 --> 00:25:39,513
Do I look like someone you know?

269
00:25:40,088 --> 00:25:41,488
How did you know?

270
00:25:41,733 --> 00:25:44,223
Actually, from the first time I saw you,

271
00:25:44,225 --> 00:25:45,654
I thought you seemed kind of familiar.

272
00:25:48,829 --> 00:25:50,033
It's because...

273
00:25:52,946 --> 00:25:54,793
I have a friendly face.

274
00:25:55,456 --> 00:25:57,054
I've heard that I look like someone...

275
00:25:57,055 --> 00:25:59,872
so many times,
I've got calluses on my ears.

276
00:26:00,073 --> 00:26:02,079
Want to see the calluses on my ears?

277
00:26:02,303 --> 00:26:03,931
No, that's okay.

278
00:26:04,619 --> 00:26:05,740
Enjoy your meal.

279
00:26:11,707 --> 00:26:14,412
- Want a drink?
- No, I'm fine.

280
00:26:14,437 --> 00:26:16,033
- Let me pour for you.
- Sure.

281
00:26:28,482 --> 00:26:29,901
Are you married already?

282
00:26:30,248 --> 00:26:32,824
The old lady who runs the shop
across the street...

283
00:26:32,849 --> 00:26:35,134
seemed to call you
"someone's mom" or something.

284
00:26:37,379 --> 00:26:42,101
I'm not married yet, but I have a son.

285
00:26:43,353 --> 00:26:45,505
You're not married, but you have a son?

286
00:26:45,939 --> 00:26:47,661
A single mom?

287
00:26:47,694 --> 00:26:49,814
Yes. That's what some people call it.

288
00:26:50,034 --> 00:26:52,947
You're really confident, boss.

289
00:26:53,811 --> 00:26:56,193
I have no reason not to be.

290
00:26:58,403 --> 00:26:59,655
What about a boyfriend?

291
00:27:02,246 --> 00:27:04,795
- I have one.
- You have a boyfriend too?

292
00:27:05,083 --> 00:27:07,264
What does he do?

293
00:27:07,279 --> 00:27:09,632
Is he rich? What's his salary?
Does he own a house?

294
00:27:09,634 --> 00:27:11,443
What do his parents do?

295
00:27:17,194 --> 00:27:18,334
Just because.

296
00:27:18,832 --> 00:27:23,768
When I see you, young and running a shop,
I feel like your big sister.

297
00:27:24,620 --> 00:27:28,632
It's like you're my little sister.

298
00:27:29,172 --> 00:27:31,474
I'm being so nosy, aren't I?

299
00:27:31,547 --> 00:27:32,547
I'm sorry.

300
00:27:33,071 --> 00:27:36,646
I love him so much.

301
00:27:37,694 --> 00:27:40,138
Just hearing his voice
makes my heart race,

302
00:27:40,858 --> 00:27:43,768
and the sound of his footsteps
makes me nervous.

303
00:27:44,760 --> 00:27:46,857
Even if I don't make him happy,

304
00:27:47,510 --> 00:27:49,624
I worry he might be unhappy because of me.

305
00:27:50,219 --> 00:27:53,414
That always scares me a little.

306
00:27:55,086 --> 00:27:58,607
Okay. I get what you're saying.

307
00:27:58,777 --> 00:28:02,374
But realistically,
if a guy lives on an overdraft...

308
00:28:02,399 --> 00:28:04,041
and can't even shop at a department store,

309
00:28:04,066 --> 00:28:06,521
you can't really like a man like that.

310
00:28:07,829 --> 00:28:09,846
No matter what kind of person he is,

311
00:28:10,147 --> 00:28:14,487
I love him, respect him, and like him.

312
00:28:14,973 --> 00:28:16,721
Even if he's a beggar?

313
00:28:17,127 --> 00:28:19,857
Yes. Even if he's an alien
or not even alive.

314
00:28:20,894 --> 00:28:25,513
Even if he's lettuce, kimchi, or garlic.

315
00:28:33,310 --> 00:28:34,904
You're smiling?

316
00:28:36,587 --> 00:28:38,007
Yun Jin called me.

317
00:28:38,032 --> 00:28:41,687
She said you signed that waiver
giving up your assets and inheritance.

318
00:28:42,508 --> 00:28:44,701
You're completely broke now.

319
00:28:44,754 --> 00:28:46,487
Why would I be broke?

320
00:28:46,621 --> 00:28:50,294
I'm healthy,
and I have a job to work hard at.

321
00:28:51,714 --> 00:28:54,050
I knew you were a fool,

322
00:28:54,387 --> 00:28:57,874
but I didn't know you were this hopeless.

323
00:28:58,904 --> 00:29:00,520
Look how happy you are.

324
00:29:01,006 --> 00:29:05,254
I call you a fool and an idiot,
and you're just happy.

325
00:29:05,441 --> 00:29:08,701
I'm going to work really hard now.

326
00:29:09,231 --> 00:29:14,745
No more slacking off.
I'm going to make money for real.

327
00:29:14,830 --> 00:29:16,006
You'd better.

328
00:29:16,388 --> 00:29:18,730
You walked away from a crazy fortune,

329
00:29:18,732 --> 00:29:22,412
so you'd better earn every penny,
even pocket change from kids.

330
00:29:22,414 --> 00:29:24,562
The group dinner reservation for 30
is today, right?

331
00:29:25,808 --> 00:29:27,650
And they're not just regular customers.

332
00:29:27,651 --> 00:29:30,424
They point cameras at everything
they chew, eat, and taste,

333
00:29:30,972 --> 00:29:33,141
and they're supposed to be super picky.

334
00:29:35,321 --> 00:29:37,406
Move. I can't just lie here right now.

335
00:29:37,431 --> 00:29:40,252
Hey, shouldn't you at least
finish your IV before you go?

336
00:29:41,680 --> 00:29:42,802
Let's go.

337
00:29:45,620 --> 00:29:47,504
He has no idea what he's thrown away.

338
00:29:55,158 --> 00:29:56,367
Welcome.

339
00:30:12,574 --> 00:30:14,645
Why are you two sitting apart?

340
00:30:15,416 --> 00:30:16,569
Did you have a fight?

341
00:30:18,445 --> 00:30:20,921
Just a bottle of soju
and a bowl of noodles.

342
00:30:23,194 --> 00:30:24,541
One order of noodles.

343
00:30:46,305 --> 00:30:50,354
It's your fault and mine
that Gyu O turned out like that.

344
00:30:51,140 --> 00:30:53,350
I'll definitely pay
for abandoning my child,

345
00:30:53,884 --> 00:30:59,153
so don't you forget. You'll pay too
for turning a blind eye to your child.

346
00:31:04,872 --> 00:31:06,121
Here's your soju.

347
00:31:44,078 --> 00:31:45,334
Why are you crying?

348
00:31:50,120 --> 00:31:53,862
- I asked why you're crying.
- Stay out of it.

349
00:31:53,888 --> 00:31:56,494
How can I stay out of it?

350
00:31:57,074 --> 00:32:02,742
You were always so bright, like a kid,
and now you're crying like it's the end.

351
00:32:05,554 --> 00:32:06,554
Forget it.

352
00:32:08,162 --> 00:32:10,427
Friend? We agreed
not to be friends anymore.

353
00:32:12,201 --> 00:32:13,254
Seriously...

354
00:32:18,308 --> 00:32:21,534
Hey, are you...

355
00:32:23,484 --> 00:32:27,121
Is this because I turned down
your proposal and hurt you?

356
00:32:28,987 --> 00:32:30,200
It's not.

357
00:32:31,500 --> 00:32:33,907
Sure looks like it is.

358
00:32:34,760 --> 00:32:37,827
You got really hurt
when I turned you down.

359
00:32:38,314 --> 00:32:41,141
For a grown man, you're so fragile.

360
00:32:43,341 --> 00:32:44,567
Go back to your seat.

361
00:32:45,047 --> 00:32:48,853
I want to be alone today.

362
00:32:50,866 --> 00:32:53,958
- Seok Jung.
- I said we're not friends.

363
00:32:54,010 --> 00:32:56,413
I'm not friends with women.

364
00:33:00,121 --> 00:33:01,338
Hong Ok Seon.

365
00:33:02,993 --> 00:33:07,341
Today, I deserve to be punished
with compound interest.

366
00:33:07,853 --> 00:33:10,081
You seem like a good, kind woman,

367
00:33:10,616 --> 00:33:15,700
so don't get hit by stones meant for me.
Treat me like a bus passing by.

368
00:33:17,554 --> 00:33:21,494
Someday, before we die,

369
00:33:21,519 --> 00:33:24,134
if we happen to meet again by chance,

370
00:33:25,358 --> 00:33:29,445
and if you're still running
the sashimi restaurant then,

371
00:33:29,633 --> 00:33:31,861
just buy me a plate of premium grouper.

372
00:33:43,387 --> 00:33:45,000
Now go back to your seat.

373
00:33:54,473 --> 00:33:56,666
Hey. Fine.

374
00:33:59,267 --> 00:34:01,933
Let's just not be friends, okay?

375
00:34:02,013 --> 00:34:04,570
Who needs friendship
between a man and a woman?

376
00:34:04,595 --> 00:34:09,108
Hey, from today, let's just flirt.

377
00:34:12,587 --> 00:34:17,120
But I'm only into platonic love.

378
00:34:17,586 --> 00:34:20,227
Holding hands is as far as it goes?

379
00:34:20,871 --> 00:34:22,080
If you agree, say "deal."

380
00:34:25,747 --> 00:34:26,760
Deal?

381
00:34:31,095 --> 00:34:32,301
Let go of me!

382
00:34:32,326 --> 00:34:34,719
Hey, you punks!

383
00:34:34,744 --> 00:34:37,031
Do you know who I am?

384
00:34:37,207 --> 00:34:41,069
I'm the chairman's in-law!

385
00:34:41,094 --> 00:34:43,635
My daughter-in-law
is the chairman's daughter!

386
00:34:44,047 --> 00:34:46,199
If you don't let me in right now,

387
00:34:46,506 --> 00:34:49,054
I'll have you all fired.

388
00:34:49,246 --> 00:34:52,706
- You can't do this here.
- Let go and let me in right now!

389
00:34:52,731 --> 00:34:54,817
It's okay. Let her go.

390
00:34:59,300 --> 00:35:00,493
Do you know me?

391
00:35:01,153 --> 00:35:03,963
No, I don't.

392
00:35:04,971 --> 00:35:06,867
Are you someone important?

393
00:35:07,347 --> 00:35:09,181
I heard you're my mother-in-law.

394
00:35:10,762 --> 00:35:12,590
I'm not even married yet,

395
00:35:12,615 --> 00:35:14,763
so where did a mother-in-law come from?

396
00:35:14,941 --> 00:35:17,074
Should I call the police
and ask them for you?

397
00:35:17,406 --> 00:35:19,208
No.

398
00:35:19,233 --> 00:35:23,033
Don't ask the police. Ask the chairman.

399
00:35:23,134 --> 00:35:26,854
He'll know if you say
it's Han Gyu Yeong's mother-in-law.

400
00:35:27,427 --> 00:35:28,587
Han Gyu Yeong?

401
00:35:30,541 --> 00:35:34,394
I'm thinking of putting the Jeju villa
up for a quick sale.

402
00:35:34,439 --> 00:35:36,025
(Chairman Jang Hun Tae)

403
00:35:36,070 --> 00:35:37,707
The land too.

404
00:35:37,732 --> 00:35:42,414
No, that's not it. I just need
some cash for personal reasons.

405
00:35:45,387 --> 00:35:49,688
Okay, look into it
and get back to me right away.

406
00:35:51,289 --> 00:35:52,313
What is it?

407
00:35:53,833 --> 00:35:56,480
A woman named Sim Su Ji
showed up in the lobby.

408
00:35:58,681 --> 00:36:00,905
Said she's your daughter's mother-in-law.

409
00:36:00,999 --> 00:36:02,394
Do you know her?

410
00:36:04,107 --> 00:36:05,220
Seo Hyeon, that's...

411
00:36:05,320 --> 00:36:07,927
And yesterday, they said
a man named Kang Sang Man came by.

412
00:36:08,001 --> 00:36:11,333
And he's apparently her father-in-law?

413
00:36:13,500 --> 00:36:16,394
You seem to know in-laws
that even I don't know about, Dad.

414
00:36:16,667 --> 00:36:20,240
And I heard you hurt your shoulder
while you were with Kang Sang Man.

415
00:36:28,754 --> 00:36:31,121
Tell whoever came to see me to leave.

416
00:36:40,466 --> 00:36:42,427
Is Han Gyu Yeong Han Gyu Rim's sister?

417
00:36:42,454 --> 00:36:44,021
Then is she Mom's daughter?

418
00:36:44,408 --> 00:36:47,761
Have you two already been
in touch with them?

419
00:36:48,848 --> 00:36:50,847
So you must have met Han Gyu Rim too?

420
00:36:51,194 --> 00:36:52,480
Since when?

421
00:36:52,703 --> 00:36:54,203
How long have you been lying to me?

422
00:36:54,228 --> 00:36:58,115
I've never lied to you.
Don't get the wrong idea.

423
00:36:58,587 --> 00:37:00,241
And your mom doesn't know.

424
00:37:02,314 --> 00:37:04,034
Your mom doesn't know anything.

425
00:37:04,361 --> 00:37:06,523
And I'll keep it that way to the end,

426
00:37:07,364 --> 00:37:09,394
so pretend you don't know
about this and let it go.

427
00:37:09,541 --> 00:37:12,572
How can I pretend I don't know?
You're hurt, Dad.

428
00:37:13,727 --> 00:37:15,462
Those people, Han Gyu Yeong's in-laws,

429
00:37:15,464 --> 00:37:18,327
seem to be threatening you
with something big.

430
00:37:21,354 --> 00:37:22,980
Should I dig into it myself?

431
00:37:23,874 --> 00:37:27,403
I don't care whether Mom finds out.
I'll even hire a private investigator...

432
00:37:27,428 --> 00:37:29,197
and dig to the very bottom. Should I?

433
00:37:29,594 --> 00:37:30,628
Seo Hyeon.

434
00:37:31,014 --> 00:37:33,580
Should I contact that girl,
Han Gyu Yeong, myself?

435
00:37:33,794 --> 00:37:36,961
Should I go confront her
and ask why she's making my dad suffer?

436
00:37:36,986 --> 00:37:38,713
Why are you talking like that?

437
00:37:40,447 --> 00:37:43,420
If she's your mom's daughter,
she's like a daughter to me too.

438
00:37:45,666 --> 00:37:47,493
Just as you're Ko Yun Hui's daughter,

439
00:37:48,114 --> 00:37:52,867
Han Gyu Rim and Han Gyu Yeong
are my daughters too.

440
00:37:57,761 --> 00:37:58,774
Okay.

441
00:38:03,372 --> 00:38:07,106
Didn't that jerk Kang Seong Uk
come to the office today?

442
00:38:07,173 --> 00:38:11,560
He didn't. Can't you just
get a restraining order or something?

443
00:38:11,653 --> 00:38:13,793
You think I don't do it
because I don't know how?

444
00:38:14,580 --> 00:38:18,213
I did some stuff too,
so I've got a guilty conscience.

445
00:38:19,254 --> 00:38:21,861
I'm about to completely lose my mind.

446
00:38:22,873 --> 00:38:24,497
Hey, I have to go.

447
00:38:33,807 --> 00:38:35,200
Sister.

448
00:38:37,640 --> 00:38:39,573
I told you I'm not a "sister," okay?

449
00:38:39,654 --> 00:38:41,287
How am I your "sister?"

450
00:38:41,541 --> 00:38:43,947
It messes up the whole family tree.

451
00:38:44,168 --> 00:38:46,383
So call me what you used to,

452
00:38:46,385 --> 00:38:48,701
"granny," like before.

453
00:38:49,421 --> 00:38:50,848
Granny.

454
00:38:50,881 --> 00:38:54,687
No, not "granny." Grandma.

455
00:38:55,394 --> 00:38:56,660
Grandma.

456
00:38:59,312 --> 00:39:01,014
Hurry and get changed.

457
00:39:01,028 --> 00:39:02,641
We have somewhere to go.

458
00:39:03,041 --> 00:39:05,180
Where? Where are we going?

459
00:39:05,373 --> 00:39:07,692
We're going to see
a fortune teller named Park...

460
00:39:07,765 --> 00:39:10,685
to find out how to bring you
back to your senses...

461
00:39:12,788 --> 00:39:15,254
Like you'd even understand if I explained.

462
00:39:15,442 --> 00:39:18,461
Hurry, get changed, and come with me.

463
00:39:19,861 --> 00:39:21,308
I don't want to go. I'm scared.

464
00:39:21,541 --> 00:39:25,320
What's so scary? Let's go. Hurry.

465
00:39:25,485 --> 00:39:29,138
I'll buy you some yummy candy,
so let's go, okay?

466
00:39:29,907 --> 00:39:31,314
No. I'm scared.

467
00:39:31,339 --> 00:39:32,999
I'm going to my room.

468
00:39:33,114 --> 00:39:35,900
You think I've got time to kill?

469
00:39:36,081 --> 00:39:39,087
I'm doing this to fix
that broken head of yours.

470
00:39:39,112 --> 00:39:40,672
No. I'm not going.

471
00:39:41,941 --> 00:39:44,714
If you keep refusing,

472
00:39:45,394 --> 00:39:48,854
I'll have a tiger come get you. Rawr!

473
00:39:49,634 --> 00:39:52,239
I don't think I'm scared of tigers.

474
00:39:53,448 --> 00:39:55,515
You're not scared of tigers?

475
00:39:57,122 --> 00:39:58,256
Right.

476
00:39:59,475 --> 00:40:02,821
- This won't work.
- Try sending a snake. Think I'll come?

477
00:40:02,914 --> 00:40:07,681
You can't get away with it forever.
If you do wrong, you must pay for it.

478
00:40:08,707 --> 00:40:12,209
I might as well call
the person she hates most,

479
00:40:12,422 --> 00:40:15,924
her father, and try some shock therapy.

480
00:40:15,949 --> 00:40:19,539
Hold on. What's Gyeol's grandpa's number?

481
00:40:19,564 --> 00:40:21,564
I'll change and be right out, Grandma.

482
00:40:24,701 --> 00:40:27,801
Buy me sweet and spicy fried chicken,
not candy.

483
00:40:31,900 --> 00:40:35,133
Did the shock therapy work or what?

484
00:40:55,647 --> 00:40:57,194
It was Unit 302, right?

485
00:40:58,801 --> 00:41:00,381
Hey, cheater.

486
00:41:06,021 --> 00:41:08,234
And paranoid husband.

487
00:41:10,920 --> 00:41:12,607
What brings you to my house?

488
00:41:12,954 --> 00:41:14,274
Here to look for Gyu Yeong?

489
00:41:14,607 --> 00:41:17,650
- Gyu Yeong's here, isn't she?
- No.

490
00:41:17,687 --> 00:41:19,180
Should I go in and search?

491
00:41:19,634 --> 00:41:21,420
What are you going to do if you find her?

492
00:41:22,508 --> 00:41:24,327
And what will you do if you don't?

493
00:41:24,352 --> 00:41:26,345
I know she's here!

494
00:41:29,494 --> 00:41:31,840
Then let's record it as proof.

495
00:41:32,621 --> 00:41:35,925
If you search and Gyu Yeong isn't here,

496
00:41:36,179 --> 00:41:38,371
you won't object if all your teeth,
implants included,

497
00:41:38,625 --> 00:41:43,351
end up replaced with full dentures.

498
00:41:44,399 --> 00:41:45,937
I'm recording now.

499
00:41:49,028 --> 00:41:50,827
If you search my house...

500
00:41:51,143 --> 00:41:55,388
and Gyu Yeong's here, I'll stand at ease
and take every hit you throw.

501
00:41:55,897 --> 00:41:57,794
But if she isn't here...

502
00:42:02,894 --> 00:42:05,054
Did I say she was definitely here?

503
00:42:06,114 --> 00:42:08,444
I just guessed she might be.

504
00:42:09,701 --> 00:42:13,256
Just because you're a bit tall,
you keep looking down on me,

505
00:42:13,505 --> 00:42:15,378
so I guess I look like a pushover.

506
00:42:15,505 --> 00:42:20,085
You don't live up to your height anyway,
so let's even out our heights.

507
00:42:21,998 --> 00:42:23,513
What are you talking about?

508
00:42:25,247 --> 00:42:28,078
If you search and Gyu Yeong isn't here,

509
00:42:28,103 --> 00:42:30,906
we agree to fold your spine in half...

510
00:42:31,190 --> 00:42:35,336
or break your legs to make you my size.

511
00:42:36,597 --> 00:42:38,094
Say "I agree."

512
00:42:39,754 --> 00:42:41,367
What, are you a psycho?

513
00:42:43,301 --> 00:42:45,350
I'm shocked. Seriously.

514
00:42:45,398 --> 00:42:49,129
Cho Heung Sik,
were you always this horrible?

515
00:42:53,633 --> 00:42:55,840
Cho Heung Sik...

516
00:43:05,701 --> 00:43:08,821
I was so scared he'd search my house.

517
00:43:11,728 --> 00:43:13,188
The blood sausage got cold.

518
00:43:14,294 --> 00:43:17,454
Evil spirits, be gone.

519
00:43:19,426 --> 00:43:23,040
Be gone. Evil spirits, be gone.

520
00:43:23,065 --> 00:43:25,538
Evil spirits, be gone.

521
00:43:26,281 --> 00:43:29,074
Be gone. Evil spirits, be gone.

522
00:43:30,394 --> 00:43:35,007
You wicked spirit, be gone at once.

523
00:43:35,032 --> 00:43:38,765
Great spirits.

524
00:43:39,185 --> 00:43:45,585
Please watch over this poor soul.

525
00:43:55,940 --> 00:43:57,107
Who are you?

526
00:44:00,467 --> 00:44:02,869
I asked who you are. What's your name?

527
00:44:06,807 --> 00:44:13,167
How dare you, in front of the spirits,
you wicked thing!

528
00:44:16,061 --> 00:44:18,594
Spirits?

529
00:44:53,241 --> 00:44:55,681
I came, so why won't you even look at me?

530
00:44:56,568 --> 00:44:59,141
Sorry, I didn't know you were here.

531
00:45:00,448 --> 00:45:03,278
- You're here earlier than I thought.
- We had a half day.

532
00:45:04,108 --> 00:45:05,601
But why a bookstore?

533
00:45:08,734 --> 00:45:10,531
Past GED exam questions?

534
00:45:12,384 --> 00:45:13,933
You're taking the GED?

535
00:45:15,694 --> 00:45:17,610
Teach me, Hui Na.

536
00:45:18,727 --> 00:45:22,187
I'll be the most rewarding student
you've ever taught.

537
00:45:23,888 --> 00:45:27,324
I was in the top five
in my class back in school.

538
00:45:29,294 --> 00:45:33,224
What do I do? I'm so touched,
I'm about to cry.

539
00:45:36,641 --> 00:45:38,718
But how do you solve this?

540
00:45:39,755 --> 00:45:41,601
The one with the absolute value...

541
00:45:57,100 --> 00:45:59,184
This is "The Mother's Dream."

542
00:45:59,209 --> 00:46:01,207
It's a poem about a mother's dream,

543
00:46:01,444 --> 00:46:04,428
and you have to choose the prepositions
that go in A and B.

544
00:46:05,527 --> 00:46:09,147
First, want to try translating
the sentence for A?

545
00:46:14,067 --> 00:46:18,333
A child I had,

546
00:46:20,060 --> 00:46:23,633
but couldn't raise.

547
00:46:25,774 --> 00:46:27,527
Good job.

548
00:46:28,048 --> 00:46:32,328
Then what preposition
goes in front of "keep?"

549
00:46:36,013 --> 00:46:37,026
To?

550
00:46:38,120 --> 00:46:40,182
You are driving me crazy.

551
00:46:40,207 --> 00:46:41,807
Why are you so smart?

552
00:46:41,954 --> 00:46:43,699
There's nothing left for me to teach you.

553
00:46:45,114 --> 00:46:48,948
Then want to try translating
the sentence for B too?

554
00:46:55,147 --> 00:46:57,680
It's okay to get it wrong. It happens.

555
00:47:00,828 --> 00:47:03,078
I wish the timing had been a little later.

556
00:47:04,641 --> 00:47:05,648
What?

557
00:47:05,801 --> 00:47:08,134
After I'd become a little more impressive,

558
00:47:10,734 --> 00:47:12,494
that would've been a better time.

559
00:47:14,267 --> 00:47:16,181
Who? Me?

560
00:47:19,180 --> 00:47:22,852
You're plenty cool and impressive,
Han Gyu O.

561
00:47:23,861 --> 00:47:26,588
I've already fallen for you
so hard I can't move,

562
00:47:26,868 --> 00:47:28,301
so how much more impressive
do you want to get?

563
00:47:35,154 --> 00:47:37,867
- I met my mom today.
- Really?

564
00:47:44,008 --> 00:47:46,240
I didn't think I'd see her this soon.

565
00:47:47,548 --> 00:47:49,014
It was way too soon.

566
00:47:50,234 --> 00:47:52,521
Of all times, she saw me
at my lowest and lamest,

567
00:47:53,367 --> 00:47:57,341
when I was most embarrassed and ashamed.

568
00:48:00,128 --> 00:48:01,221
Past tense.

569
00:48:02,874 --> 00:48:05,527
That's past tense, not present tense.

570
00:48:09,187 --> 00:48:11,434
What did my mom dream of for me?

571
00:48:14,488 --> 00:48:16,333
What did she want me to become?

572
00:48:17,608 --> 00:48:19,900
What kind of life did she want me to live?

573
00:48:37,194 --> 00:48:38,537
When did you even take this?

574
00:48:38,730 --> 00:48:42,868
Yesterday, before we met the lady,
while you were texting Dae Ung.

575
00:48:44,054 --> 00:48:45,063
Why did you take this?

576
00:48:45,461 --> 00:48:49,018
Just because. I could show Gyu Rim
in case she ever wants to see her.

577
00:48:49,581 --> 00:48:51,668
It's her mom's face.
She shouldn't forget it.

578
00:48:51,881 --> 00:48:54,834
No. Nobody can find out
we're seeing the lady yet.

579
00:48:55,780 --> 00:48:57,997
That's why I said "in case."

580
00:48:58,354 --> 00:48:59,748
They haven't seen each other in 17 years.

581
00:49:00,451 --> 00:49:03,136
If she gets any older, Gyu Rim might fail
to recognize her even face to face.

582
00:49:03,161 --> 00:49:04,194
Look at separated families.

583
00:49:09,008 --> 00:49:13,421
But don't you think we look a bit
like the lady around the ears?

584
00:49:14,648 --> 00:49:16,508
Why would the lady look like us?

585
00:49:16,533 --> 00:49:17,648
Look closely.

586
00:49:18,340 --> 00:49:20,181
Her eyebrows look just like yours.

587
00:49:21,098 --> 00:49:25,227
Sure. Maybe our toes look alike too.

588
00:49:25,858 --> 00:49:29,134
Don't you think her smile
looks a little like mine?

589
00:49:31,213 --> 00:49:32,569
Let's stop, Han Gyu Seo.

590
00:49:33,391 --> 00:49:34,700
- Han Gyu Seo.
- Yeah?

591
00:49:36,474 --> 00:49:38,394
What, you two are together. Perfect.

592
00:49:39,008 --> 00:49:42,128
Some lady told me to give this to you two.

593
00:49:42,301 --> 00:49:43,640
- What lady?
- What lady?

594
00:49:44,341 --> 00:49:46,874
I don't know.
I met her at the school gate.

595
00:49:47,467 --> 00:49:50,379
Any other Han Gyu Seo and Han Gyu Min
twins at our school besides you?

596
00:49:50,994 --> 00:49:51,994
What are you doing? Take it.

597
00:49:52,680 --> 00:49:53,681
- What is it?
- What is it?

598
00:49:53,834 --> 00:49:55,361
How should I know?

599
00:49:55,414 --> 00:49:57,181
- Hurry, I need to go to the bathroom.
- Okay.

600
00:49:58,934 --> 00:50:00,749
What is it? A fan of mine?

601
00:50:03,657 --> 00:50:08,041
There's something bulky inside,
and a letter too.

602
00:50:08,066 --> 00:50:09,554
- Give it here.
- It must really be a fan.

603
00:50:18,854 --> 00:50:23,240
To my beloved son and daughter,
Gyu Seo and Gyu Min.

604
00:50:23,908 --> 00:50:26,874
What? That crazy stalker from last time?

605
00:50:27,375 --> 00:50:30,535
Kids, it's been so long.

606
00:50:31,798 --> 00:50:33,628
Hey, Han Gyu Seo.

607
00:50:33,901 --> 00:50:37,428
It's me, your mom.

608
00:50:40,121 --> 00:50:45,113
The mom who carried you for nine months
and gave birth to you.

609
00:50:46,867 --> 00:50:52,101
I missed you so much
that I cried myself to sleep every night.

610
00:50:52,701 --> 00:50:57,614
I missed you so much
that life didn't feel like living.

611
00:50:59,634 --> 00:51:01,474
You're all grown up now,

612
00:51:01,528 --> 00:51:04,915
so I believe you'll understand
and forgive me.

613
00:51:05,701 --> 00:51:09,963
The enclosed money is my way
of saying I'm sorry.

614
00:51:10,649 --> 00:51:16,053
Buy anything you've wanted
or wished you could have.

615
00:51:16,948 --> 00:51:20,001
I'm always watching over you.

616
00:51:21,074 --> 00:51:24,041
I'll be waiting for the day we meet soon.

617
00:51:24,651 --> 00:51:29,848
Love, your mom, who loves you
more than anything in the world.

618
00:51:32,948 --> 00:51:34,015
Where are you?

619
00:51:34,681 --> 00:51:37,568
Come out. Come out right now.

620
00:51:40,441 --> 00:51:41,794
Mom? Who's my mom?

621
00:51:42,595 --> 00:51:44,334
How dare you call yourself that?

622
00:51:45,741 --> 00:51:47,348
Come out right now,
take this, and get lost.

623
00:51:47,841 --> 00:51:50,841
I don't need this,
so take it and get lost right now.

624
00:51:52,431 --> 00:51:54,614
Mom? Who's my mom? Seriously?

625
00:51:55,285 --> 00:51:58,214
I don't need a mom like you, so get lost.

626
00:51:58,941 --> 00:52:01,954
Han Gyu Seo, stop it. Please.

627
00:52:02,570 --> 00:52:05,294
Gyu Seo, stop it.

628
00:52:06,555 --> 00:52:09,179
Stop. Let's stop and go inside, okay?

629
00:52:09,594 --> 00:52:12,456
Our mom abandoned us,
cheated, and ran off.

630
00:52:12,481 --> 00:52:14,641
Do you want the whole school,
the whole world, to know?

631
00:52:16,815 --> 00:52:18,268
What if Gyu Rim finds out?

632
00:52:18,894 --> 00:52:21,288
What will you do if she hears the rumors?

633
00:52:21,381 --> 00:52:22,648
Please, let's go inside.

634
00:52:24,801 --> 00:52:26,314
Let's go.

635
00:52:28,458 --> 00:52:31,444
(Seonghan High School)

636
00:52:50,894 --> 00:52:53,575
Han Seok Jung.

637
00:52:54,067 --> 00:52:56,732
How on earth did you raise my son?

638
00:52:56,988 --> 00:52:59,221
Why is he such a thug?

639
00:52:59,747 --> 00:53:03,059
He's about to eat me alive.

640
00:53:22,037 --> 00:53:24,705
Are you crazy? Why throw away money?

641
00:53:25,033 --> 00:53:26,958
Why would you take money from that woman?

642
00:53:27,713 --> 00:53:29,269
Does money have someone's name on it?

643
00:53:29,294 --> 00:53:30,443
If you don't want it, forget it.

644
00:53:30,468 --> 00:53:31,848
I'll keep all of it myself.

645
00:53:31,873 --> 00:53:33,848
Han Gyu Min, bring that back right now.

646
00:53:33,873 --> 00:53:36,149
Half of it's mine. Then give me my half.

647
00:53:36,204 --> 00:53:38,381
I'm taking the money,
but I'm not forgiving her.

648
00:53:38,406 --> 00:53:40,781
I won't accept her as my mom either.
She gave it on her own terms,

649
00:53:40,806 --> 00:53:42,281
so I'll do what I want too. So what?

650
00:53:56,794 --> 00:53:58,874
- Want to try this one?
- Sure.

651
00:54:01,099 --> 00:54:02,714
- Is the temperature okay?
- Yes.

652
00:54:03,601 --> 00:54:06,828
This is so nice. It's super warm.

653
00:54:07,019 --> 00:54:08,527
Nothing beats nice and toasty.

654
00:54:08,748 --> 00:54:11,183
A lot of people with poor circulation
come looking for it,

655
00:54:11,208 --> 00:54:13,288
so it's the most popular product
in our store.

656
00:54:13,828 --> 00:54:15,734
- Really?
- Yeah.

657
00:54:15,834 --> 00:54:18,054
Hey, Han Gyu Seo. This one seems good.

658
00:54:18,398 --> 00:54:21,941
Your father comes here
and warms up every chance he gets.

659
00:54:21,966 --> 00:54:23,675
He says it warms him right up.

660
00:54:23,708 --> 00:54:26,088
Your father's had his eye on this one.

661
00:54:26,155 --> 00:54:27,361
He'll love it.

662
00:54:27,461 --> 00:54:28,761
It's not for our dad.

663
00:54:28,786 --> 00:54:31,988
- Then for Gyu Rim?
- Yes.

664
00:54:33,101 --> 00:54:36,081
You two are really buying this as a gift?

665
00:54:37,281 --> 00:54:41,554
Yes. We kind of struck it rich
out of nowhere.

666
00:54:42,009 --> 00:54:45,425
Did you win the lottery? Really?

667
00:54:45,657 --> 00:54:46,688
Yes.

668
00:54:47,534 --> 00:54:50,716
But you can never tell our dad.

669
00:54:52,374 --> 00:54:57,272
But if we give it to her,
we don't think Gyu Rim would take it.

670
00:54:57,494 --> 00:54:59,655
Is there any way to make it work?

671
00:55:01,674 --> 00:55:05,854
Don't ask me to do anything
that takes brains.

672
00:55:06,981 --> 00:55:10,168
A ticking time bomb
just rolled into my house,

673
00:55:10,240 --> 00:55:12,033
so my head's already about to explode.

674
00:55:13,744 --> 00:55:14,933
What should we do?

675
00:55:15,034 --> 00:55:17,294
Scheming is our dad's specialty.

676
00:55:17,319 --> 00:55:19,261
But we can't ask him about this.

677
00:55:19,627 --> 00:55:20,668
I know.

678
00:55:24,008 --> 00:55:26,206
What? You won what?

679
00:55:26,384 --> 00:55:30,061
A prize, Mom. They said it's a mat.

680
00:55:32,191 --> 00:55:35,308
The department store's giving away prizes
for its 300th anniversary.

681
00:55:35,608 --> 00:55:38,468
Not 300th. 30th.

682
00:55:38,493 --> 00:55:40,688
- Right, 30th.
- Yeah.

683
00:55:40,713 --> 00:55:42,888
Anyway, Gyu Seo entered, and he won.

684
00:55:42,954 --> 00:55:44,014
No way.

685
00:55:45,850 --> 00:55:47,618
Congratulations, Gyu Seo.

686
00:55:47,643 --> 00:55:50,432
You're the first person I know
who's ever won something like this.

687
00:55:50,488 --> 00:55:55,040
Me too. You're the first person
I know who's ever won.

688
00:55:55,867 --> 00:55:58,247
Anyway, I want to give it to you.

689
00:55:59,214 --> 00:56:00,284
- Me?
- Yeah.

690
00:56:00,427 --> 00:56:04,554
Yeah. You work so hard, and we didn't
even pay for it. We won it.

691
00:56:04,695 --> 00:56:07,062
- Take it, Gyu Rim.
- Take it, Mom.

692
00:56:07,578 --> 00:56:10,568
I'm fine. I'm still young. Give it to Dad.

693
00:56:10,593 --> 00:56:11,661
Absolutely not.

694
00:56:12,121 --> 00:56:14,905
It's being delivered soon,
so don't ever tell Dad.

695
00:56:15,374 --> 00:56:16,994
- Gyu Seo.
- Dad better not be home.

696
00:56:17,019 --> 00:56:19,374
- He'd take it right away.
- Gyu Min.

697
00:56:35,208 --> 00:56:36,241
Dad.

698
00:56:37,608 --> 00:56:39,061
You use it, Dad.

699
00:56:39,934 --> 00:56:42,754
I'm fine.
Of course you should use it, Dad.

700
00:56:43,955 --> 00:56:46,504
It's yours, Gyu Rim. You use it.

701
00:56:47,768 --> 00:56:49,708
You had it harder
than anyone in our family.

702
00:56:50,415 --> 00:56:53,715
Mom abandoned us, but you fed us milk,
changed our diapers,

703
00:56:54,101 --> 00:56:56,948
carried us, dressed us, put us to sleep,
worked, and earned money.

704
00:56:57,635 --> 00:56:59,501
You had it harder
than anyone in our family.

705
00:57:01,640 --> 00:57:03,449
Dad, do you want to say something too?

706
00:57:05,775 --> 00:57:07,348
That I had a hard time getting by too.

707
00:57:08,368 --> 00:57:10,634
I didn't do anything right, but I tried.

708
00:57:11,028 --> 00:57:13,908
I could've abandoned all of you
and started a new life on my own,

709
00:57:13,974 --> 00:57:16,074
but at least I didn't do
something that low.

710
00:57:17,115 --> 00:57:18,481
Especially with the twins,

711
00:57:18,885 --> 00:57:22,791
you carried both of them
when they had high fevers and nearly died,

712
00:57:23,058 --> 00:57:25,828
went to 20 hospitals
from night until dawn,

713
00:57:26,820 --> 00:57:29,280
and barely saved them.
You should tell them that too.

714
00:57:32,171 --> 00:57:33,454
I did that?

715
00:57:37,309 --> 00:57:38,821
When was that?

716
00:57:40,521 --> 00:57:41,931
When the twins were four.

717
00:57:42,285 --> 00:57:46,568
Back then. Right. I remember now.

718
00:57:46,760 --> 00:57:49,434
Yeah, that's right. I saved the kids.

719
00:57:49,708 --> 00:57:52,208
I saved the twins.

720
00:57:52,554 --> 00:57:56,614
I did do something
for my kids as a father.

721
00:58:07,807 --> 00:58:08,975
What?

722
00:58:13,674 --> 00:58:14,976
Hey.

723
00:58:17,028 --> 00:58:20,564
- I'm off to work.
- Hey, twins, you should hear more.

724
00:58:20,827 --> 00:58:23,308
Why are you leaving? Come on.

725
00:58:24,548 --> 00:58:26,848
You should've told
that great story sooner.

726
00:58:26,873 --> 00:58:28,154
Why are you only telling it now?

727
00:58:28,834 --> 00:58:31,010
I'm sorry. It suddenly came back to me.

728
00:58:31,274 --> 00:58:33,181
Keep thinking.

729
00:58:33,373 --> 00:58:35,893
There might be more good things I did.

730
00:58:36,001 --> 00:58:38,403
There could be more hidden good deeds.

731
00:58:39,035 --> 00:58:40,480
Okay.

732
00:58:41,021 --> 00:58:45,148
- Gyeol, you're so touched by me, right?
- Yes.

733
00:58:45,294 --> 00:58:49,034
- You totally respect me, right?
- I'm just touched.

734
00:58:49,414 --> 00:58:51,074
You're your mother's son, all right.

735
00:58:53,014 --> 00:58:56,191
Then I'll proudly take the prize.

736
00:58:56,947 --> 00:58:57,981
Okay.

737
00:59:01,454 --> 00:59:03,121
Hey, it must be here.

738
00:59:05,434 --> 00:59:06,851
It's all installed.

739
00:59:07,128 --> 00:59:08,781
Okay, thank you.

740
00:59:08,834 --> 00:59:10,754
If you have any questions,
feel free to contact us anytime.

741
00:59:10,794 --> 00:59:13,421
- Sure.
- Stay healthy.

742
00:59:13,446 --> 00:59:15,641
- Goodbye.
- Thank you.

743
00:59:15,666 --> 00:59:16,774
Have some coffee.

744
00:59:19,514 --> 00:59:23,394
So it's you.

745
00:59:23,481 --> 00:59:27,528
They say if you wish for it,
it comes true. We finally meet.

746
00:59:27,553 --> 00:59:28,921
You pretty thing.

747
00:59:29,468 --> 00:59:31,028
Like this...

748
00:59:31,628 --> 00:59:34,541
This is great.

749
00:59:34,894 --> 00:59:38,648
All that stress is melting away.
Melting away.

750
00:59:48,441 --> 00:59:51,471
- Hey, Gyu Min.
- What do I do, Gyu Rim?

751
00:59:52,801 --> 00:59:54,402
What's wrong? What happened?

752
00:59:54,701 --> 00:59:57,389
All of our restaurant staff are gone.

753
00:59:58,105 --> 01:00:01,528
Everyone except me.
I mean, except me, Mu Jin, and Jeong Woo.

754
01:00:01,828 --> 01:00:03,675
The chefs, the kitchen assistants,

755
01:00:03,914 --> 01:00:07,008
and even the part-time servers
all disappeared at once.

756
01:00:07,148 --> 01:00:08,168
Without a word.

757
01:00:08,708 --> 01:00:09,881
What do you mean?

758
01:00:45,947 --> 01:00:48,881
Mu Jin, this won't work. Let's just close.

759
01:00:49,341 --> 01:00:50,661
How are you going to do
all this by yourself?

760
01:00:50,686 --> 01:00:52,134
We're even fully booked today.

761
01:00:52,368 --> 01:00:54,341
How can I turn away customers
with reservations?

762
01:00:54,927 --> 01:00:56,300
I'll do as much as I can.

763
01:00:56,361 --> 01:00:58,941
This isn't some cooking show.
There's no way you can do it alone.

764
01:00:59,101 --> 01:01:02,254
Not even a TV chef could pull this off.
Mu Jin.

765
01:01:05,028 --> 01:01:06,391
Bring me a bandage and some disinfectant.

766
01:01:24,001 --> 01:01:27,201
You don't have to worry
about finding work.

767
01:01:27,935 --> 01:01:30,071
There should be three business cards
in the envelope.

768
01:01:30,268 --> 01:01:33,388
You can go work at whichever
of the three places you want.

769
01:01:33,901 --> 01:01:37,408
The pay and conditions
will be way better than at your last job.

770
01:01:39,035 --> 01:01:41,954
You don't need to feel guilty.

771
01:01:42,668 --> 01:01:45,697
In the end, you'll be helping the chef.

772
01:01:48,488 --> 01:01:51,302
Everything's ready for the next step,
right?

773
01:02:10,981 --> 01:02:13,917
- What?
- How far are you going to go?

774
01:02:14,528 --> 01:02:17,917
You've already taken everything
from Mu Jin, just like you wanted.

775
01:02:19,207 --> 01:02:20,991
Mu Jin still has plenty.

776
01:02:22,961 --> 01:02:24,981
Are you really trying
to leave Mu Jin with nothing?

777
01:02:25,308 --> 01:02:26,715
Once someone hits rock bottom,

778
01:02:27,474 --> 01:02:30,762
that's when you see who they really are.

779
01:02:32,635 --> 01:02:34,444
Are you testing Han Gyu Rim?

780
01:02:35,028 --> 01:02:37,468
To see if she'll still feel the same
even if Mu Jin becomes a beggar?

781
01:02:37,573 --> 01:02:39,811
Hey, just pick one.

782
01:02:40,254 --> 01:02:43,248
Either be the nice sister
or the ambitious sister.

783
01:02:43,681 --> 01:02:46,445
If you're going to be the nice sister,
you're out too.

784
01:02:50,529 --> 01:02:51,921
Just this once. Please?

785
01:02:52,425 --> 01:02:53,883
Just help me out this once.

786
01:02:53,908 --> 01:02:55,987
You know I'm desperate if I'm calling you.

787
01:03:00,308 --> 01:03:02,528
You said your restaurant
isn't busy anyway.

788
01:03:02,968 --> 01:03:04,801
Can't you close just for today and help?

789
01:03:05,074 --> 01:03:06,588
And Mu Jin? You know what he did?

790
01:03:06,961 --> 01:03:09,028
He closed his restaurant for a week
and went to help you.

791
01:03:09,053 --> 01:03:10,448
You shameless jerk.

792
01:03:11,295 --> 01:03:13,654
You're not even worth cursing at.
Get lost.

793
01:03:23,074 --> 01:03:24,858
Do you have a spare chef's uniform?

794
01:03:25,235 --> 01:03:27,229
- Gyu Rim.
- Gyu Rim.

795
01:04:00,389 --> 01:04:01,841
Hey, I think you were right.

796
01:04:02,283 --> 01:04:03,787
This is too much for one person.

797
01:04:05,066 --> 01:04:07,443
That's why I'm here.

798
01:04:17,276 --> 01:04:18,534
Gyu Rim.

799
01:04:19,768 --> 01:04:23,054
You know I'm a good cook, right?
I'll help.

800
01:05:14,908 --> 01:05:16,495
(Love on the Menu)

801
01:05:16,520 --> 01:05:18,514
How does my mom know Han Gyu O?

802
01:05:18,539 --> 01:05:20,323
- Han Gyu O?
- Is Han Gyu O a gigolo by any chance?

803
01:05:20,348 --> 01:05:22,461
- It's okay, Gyu O.
- Gyu Rim can't ever find out.

804
01:05:22,486 --> 01:05:24,166
Right, Gyu Rim can't ever find out.

805
01:05:24,287 --> 01:05:25,561
Brace yourself before you go.

806
01:05:25,586 --> 01:05:27,171
We asked for too little.

807
01:05:27,196 --> 01:05:28,608
Just give us ten million dollars.

808
01:05:28,633 --> 01:05:31,391
- Then sue us.
- Why on earth are they doing this to you?

809
01:05:31,416 --> 01:05:32,416
Why did you do that?

810
01:05:32,441 --> 01:05:33,486
Gyu Rim.

811
01:05:33,511 --> 01:05:36,500
This is the end. It's over now.

812
01:05:37,067 --> 01:05:40,214
Hello.
I have something to promise you, Mu Jin.

813
01:05:41,969 --> 01:05:43,769
Dramaday.me
